# Attrition {#sec-attrition}

As part of their service civique, each volunteer is asked to fill out three different questionnaires: the first one at the onset of their service civique (later on referred to as "q1"), the second one at the end ("q2"), and the third one six months after their service civique ("q3"). Answering these questionnaires is voluntary, and response rates typically decline considerably from the first to the third questionnaire. These declining response rates are referred to as "attrition". Some volunteers do not even respond to any one questionnaire^[Unis-Cité nevertheless has some administrative data on volunteers who did not respond to a single questionnaire, for example which program they have been in. In some of the plots in this report, notably in @sec-attrition, these volunteers appear under the label "q0".]. 

Attrition can have many causes. Here we distinguish between two explanations: ruptures, i.e. volunteers ending their service civique early (@sec-rupture) and survey fatigue, i.e. volunteers who continue their service civique but do not fill out the questionnaires (@fig-attrition-norupture). 

@fig-attrition shows attrition generally, while @fig-attrition-norupture excludes ruptures, thereby giving an estimate of survey fatigue. This latter figure shows that survey fatigue is an issue, but also suggests that there is a slightly positive trend towards reduced survey fatigue: more and more volunteers seem to be answering the questionnaires at least for the first two questionnaires (q1 and q2), but less so for the third questionnaire (q3). 


::: {#fig-attrition .cell layout-ncol="2"}
::: {.cell-output-display}
![(absolute numbers)](report.en_files/figure-docx/fig-attrition-1.png){#fig-attrition-1}
:::

::: {.cell-output-display}
![(percentages)](report.en_files/figure-docx/fig-attrition-2.png){#fig-attrition-2}
:::

Number of volunteers per survey time point. Volunteers who appear under 'q0' have participated in the program but have not even filled out the first questionnaire (q1). Note that in the percentage plot, the percentages are relative to all volunteers from the respective promo. This plot **includes** ruptures.
:::



::: {#fig-attrition-norupture .cell layout-ncol="2"}
