### Which demographic factors are associated with change of voting intentions? 

To determine which demographic variables are associated with change of voting intentions, we ran statistical models. These models are explained in the Appendix (@sec-appendix-voting). Here, we only report the variables that were statistically significant in these models.

Note that these analyses pool all cohorts. As shown above, changes in voting behavior differed considerably between cohorts (likely depending on the election calendar), so the pooled associations reported here do not tell us which volunteers changed in a particular year. Running these analyses separately by cohort would be possible, but would considerably lengthen the report.


::: {.cell}

:::


#### Sex

As shown in @fig-vote_derniers_elections-sex, more female volunteers changed towards "Yes" than towards "No". Among male volunteers, the opposite was true. 


::: {#fig-vote_derniers_elections-sex .cell layout-ncol="2"}
