:::


On a side note, looking at the 16 to 17 age groups shows that some answers were erroneous. In France, the legal voting age is 18. Therefore, the 16 to 17 year-olds, at least at the beginning of their service civique (q0/q1), have never been on a voting list before. However, as shown in @fig-vote_derniers_elections-youngest there are 443 volunteers who answered "No" at q0/q1 (which technically is true, but not the most specific answer option), and 20 who answered "Yes" (probably not reading the question carefully or accidentally clicking on the wrong response). 


::: {.cell}
