#### Zone of Residence

@fig-vote_derniers_elections-residence shows that volunteers from "QPV" and "ZRR" residential areas had a greater tendency to change towards "No", compared to "Yes". By contrast, in particular in rural areas, but also slightly in urban ones, more volunteers changed towards "Yes". Note that, as for all demographic factors in this report, these are bivariate associations, and the groups overlap: for example, volunteers from "QPV" zones are also less educated on average (50% "infra bac", compared to 36% among volunteers from urban zones). The patterns for individual variables should therefore not be interpreted in isolation. 


